cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Cascadia Listening Post"
message: >-
  If you refer to a detection report from this site, please cite the specific
  report rather than the site as a whole. Each report carries its own run
  identifiers, model versions and effective licence in its report.json.
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  Wildlife detection reports produced from continuously monitored public media
  feeds in the Salish Sea and at Mount Rainier National Park. Hydrophone audio is
  analysed for killer whale call presence and ecotype consistency; webcam and
  underwater video is analysed for animal presence. Each report publishes the
  evidence alongside the detection, states the false-positive floor measured at
  that site for that label, and reports hours of usable signal so that absence of
  detections can be distinguished from absence of recording.
authors:
  - family-names: Rain
    given-names: Brian
repository-code: "https://github.com/rain-Brian/wildlife-detections"
url: "https://rain-Brian.github.io/wildlife-detections/"
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://github.com/rain-Brian/wildlife-detections/blob/main/LICENSE"
keywords:
  - bioacoustics
  - passive acoustic monitoring
  - killer whale
  - Southern Resident
  - Salish Sea
  - camera trap
  - wildlife detection
  - machine learning
references:
  - type: data
    title: "Orcasound hydrophone network"
    abstract: >-
      Hydrophone audio used under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Reports derived from this
      audio are licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 rather than CC BY 4.0.
    url: "https://www.orcasound.net"
    license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
    authors:
      - name: "Orcasound"
  - type: data
    title: "Mount Rainier National Park webcams"
    abstract: >-
      Webcam imagery, a United States Government work in the public domain.
    url: "https://www.nps.gov/mora/learn/photosmultimedia/webcams.htm"
    authors:
      - name: "National Park Service, Mount Rainier National Park"
